"""lab-slack-listen: answers mentions of the lab's bot and direct messages in Slack (Socket Mode).

Started by hpc's crontab (under flock, so one copy runs). Needs, per workspace in /srv/lab/slack.conf,
the bot token (~/.config/lab/slack-<ws>.token) and an app-level token (~/.config/lab/slack-<ws>.apptoken).

Who is who: people link their own Slack account to a GitHub or GitLab handle in a direct message
("link github <handle>" or "link gitlab <handle>"), proving it by putting a one-time code in that
account (GitHub: a comment on an issue in the organization, or the bio; GitLab: status message). Links are
kept in /srv/lab/state/slack/people.json; `person` lines in slack.conf also count.

Authority: the PI, and for a project the people under "People" in its AGENTS.md (handles are GitHub
unless written gitlab:<handle>), may give instructions. Anyone else in a connected channel gets
answers about that channel's project only, rate-limited, and their requests count as information.
"""
